2026-09-01T14:01Z claude note the auto_vacuum trap is worse than SPEC.md 5.2.2 states, and the sentence would have misled an implementer. Measured on SQLite 3.51.3: PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL writes the header too, so auto_vacuum set AFTER WAL is lost with no table in the file yet (wal-then-av gives 0, av-then-wal gives 2). Copying v1's openHandle() order -- busy_timeout, WAL, synchronous -- and appending auto_vacuum would have silently lost incremental vacuum forever. The implemented order is busy_timeout, auto_vacuum, WAL, synchronous, foreign_keys, and a third test pins the WAL-first case red. Worth propagating into SPEC.md 5.2.2's wording as a separate ticket.
